<!--Post: 11140--><!--Time: 1110468908-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11140"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Icyou<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Icyou<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 7:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I live in Salina, KS, about 45 min. away from Park city straight up I-35.  Anyway, back in 1993 there was a woman named Kathryn Adam who was murdered at her storage unit on Centennial road here.  Centennial road is very accessible from I-35...you come off the ramp, take a left, go about 3/4 mile and take a right onto Centennial road where the storage unit is about 1/2 mile from there.  This woman was murdered presumably at her storage unit because blood was found at the unit, and her L&#39;eggs van that she drove was taken and dumped in Russel&#39;s Restaurant parking lot which is about 3 miles up Centennial Road from this particular storage unit.  Her body has never been found.  I was driving South on Centennial Road yesterday and noticed that there is a &#34;curve in road&#34; sign exactly like the one that BTK left the Post Toasties box at that is right in front of the storage unit.  My thought is...is it possible he could have killed here in Salina, too? The only similarity in the case is that her van was taken and left at a different location.  But on the day he was arrested I brought up in chat that maybe he had a storage unit somewhere that he kept his &#34;treasures&#34; in.  With the drop of the Post Toasties box, maybe it was inferring that the police would find many more of the victims&#39; belongings near one of the &#34;curve in road&#34; signs.  It might be worth it to police to check it out.  It is not unreasonable to think he could have killed in Salina, too.  Salina itself and particularly this storage unit would be just a safe enough distance yet very accessible to BTK to keep evidence in.  The only thing that bothers me is, if he left his own vehicle at Russel&#39;s Restaurant, it is quite a walk to the storage unit, although it is a straight shot.  BUT near Russel&#39;s Restaurant is another on-ramp to I-35 leading back to Park City. <BR> <BR>Footnote:  I&#39;m sure this has no relevance, but is a little creepy....there is a storage unit #666 directly facing Centennial Road.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11140-->
<!--Post: 11144--><!--Time: 1110472337-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11144"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Icyou<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Icyou<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 8:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I forgot to add...Dennis Rader attended Kansas Wesleyan University here in Salina which would prove he has a knowledge of the city.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11144-->
<!--Post: 11149--><!--Time: 1110478483-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11149"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lctrip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lctrip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 10:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Icyou - I think at this point any unsolved murder, especially of a female, within an hour&#39;s drive of Wichita needs to be seriously studied for possible connections to Rader.  This one certainly.  A L&#39;eggs van?  Pantyhose?  Boggles the mind.  Rader having a storage unit there would be a pretty simple thing for LE to run down.  I would be surprised if Salina LE isn&#39;t already working on eliminating or confirming Rader as the perp. <BR> <BR>There have been rumours that a plea bargain might be in the works.  I have several strong feelings about that; one, there will be a promise of no death penalty - just life in prison. Secondly, Rader will come clean on EVERYTHING he knows which I suspect will involve more than the 10 victims we know of, there will have been killings since 1994 when the death penalty was reinstated in KS, and that some of those will have occured outside the Wichita area. <BR> <BR>Just my opinion.....<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11149-->
<!--Post: 11154--><!--Time: 1110480413-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11154"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Icyou<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Icyou<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 10:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lctrip....man!  I didn&#39;t even think of the L&#39;eggs connection.  But yeah, she drove a van for L&#39;eggs pantyhose.  Can&#39;t believe I didn&#39;t think about the significance of that <IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0>  I was too focused on the roadsign and the proximity of the murder to I-35.  How do I bring this up to WPD, or SPD without sounding like a whack?  I&#39;m sure Rader would have rented the unit under a different name..SPD should check out people who have had long-term rental contracts with that place.  I can&#39;t remember the exact name of the place, I&#39;ll have to drive by again.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11154-->
<!--Post: 11155--><!--Time: 1110481178-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11155"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Icyou<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Icyou<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 10:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Would just like to clarify....that&#39;s I-135....growing up here, I am just accustomed to calling it I-35.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
