<!--Post: 14230--><!--Time: 1125501979-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST14230"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, August 31, 2005 - 8:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Kathryn Adam, Kathryn Bright, a Kathryn A and B. <BR> <BR>She was a route salesperson, route salespeople have ROUTines. his favorite type. <BR> <BR>Last seen at a kwik trip, a btk call made to a  <BR>kwik trip. <BR> <BR>Says he almost got stuck one time at boy scout camp, her van was covered in mud. <BR> <BR>The storage unit 666 directly across from Kathryn&#39;s is strange also. Could it be the motherlode, in an assumed name. <BR> <BR>Keep your eyes open for those sales they have <BR>when someone quits paying thier rent. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 14230-->
<!--Post: 14232--><!--Time: 1125539396-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST14232"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Icyou<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Icyou<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, August 31, 2005 - 6:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Itty,  the storage unit 666 wasn&#39;t across from her&#39;s...it just faces centennial road..anyway, I totally agree with the rest about the routine and all.  Plus, she was a saleswoman for L&#39;eggs pantyhose.  how could he resist?  although, this did take place extremely early in the morning.  There&#39;s a lot of things about it that don&#39;t make sense to me, but most things do...hence Marine Hedge...how the hell does all the trouble he went through to murder her make sense? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 14232-->
<!--Post: 14277--><!--Time: 1125764938-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST14277"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, September 03, 2005 - 9:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wichita Eagle - May 4, 1993 - 3D CITY AND STATE <BR> <BR>BLOODSTAINED VAN SETS OFF SEARCH FOR SALINA WOMAN   <BR>  SALINA Police searched for a missing woman after finding her bloodstained van last week. Kathryn Adam, 35, of Salina, was reported missing Wednesday by her daughter. Her van was found Friday in the parking lot of a restaurant that was closed for remodeling. Adam was a saleswoman for Legg&#39;s hosiery, and her van carried the Legg&#39;s logo. A large amount of blood was found Thursday at a building in west Salina where Adam went each morning to pick up stock. Police have questioned the ...  END <BR> <BR>No scout camp at this time, this says her daughter reported her missing on a Wednesday, doe network says last seen Thursday 4-29-93. <BR> <BR>She went there each day, probably at the same time. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 14277-->
