</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, September 03, 2005 - 1:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If Rader saw a panty hose truck with a favorable victim who followed a routine I have absolutely no doubt that he would take note. If he took note he would stalk. He might even strike up conversation with her and find out that she operated out of a storage shed and loaded her truck each morning.  <BR> <BR>Given his admitted &#34;thing&#34; about barns and silos &#40;wanting to convert them into torture chambers&#41;, I think that a woman who represents panyhose, alone early in the morning, on a predictable schedule, at an isolated &#34;shed type building&#34; full of pantyhose just might bring out the BTK in him. Even if it did take him a bit &#40;90 min round trip&#41; out of his way. <BR> <BR>Being a route saleswoman she was probably outgoing. So all he would really have to do would be to ask her where the Legg&#39;s factory or warehouse was. Unless she was suspicious of him she would probably explain her basic setup just to be friendly. Rader would take it from there. <BR> <BR>It would probably be irrisistable to him. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
