</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, September 06, 2005 - 12:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If the information I have found online is accurate the facts that increase the chance that 83707 did this crime are:  1-his brother lived in Fallon &#40;sp?&#41; Kansas at the time; 2-Fallon is directly west of I-35 just a few miles from an exit; 3-The storage facility where the crime occurred is within a half-mile of the interstate; 4-The exit which one takes to go to the storage facility is 1 or 2 miles north of the exit to take to Fallon. <BR>Did 83707 ever go up to visit his brother during the middle of the week?  It is not much more than an hours drive each way.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
